         * In the Kendo upgrade to 2018R1 (see API-13540) kendo changed the String parser
         * so that it converted a string value of "null" to null. We do not want this
         * (see PLV-5433). So here we use our own string parser function instead. And
         * our parser function is the same as Kendo's function prior to the 2018R1
         * upgrade.
         *
         * Dates:
         * When UTC data is bound to a Kendo grid that has a column specified as a "date" column then
         * Kendo automatically converts the UTC date value to a local date value. So for example,
         * if the UTC value is "2016-08-12T00:00:00.000Z" then in California timezone the screen
         * would display 8/11/2016 (one day behind). That is a correct conversion to local time
         * but for our date values there is no time zone associated with them so we really need to
         * display the raw UTC value 8/12/2016. So this function replaces the Kendo date parsing
         * function with our own function for date fields. Our parse function does not do the
         * conversion to local time but instead leaves the date as-is.
         */
        private replaceParseFunctions;
